// How listed goods are priced from the item value table (docs/trading.md, "Trade list format").
// A trader asks an item's value x "sell" and its list buys it at value x "buy", both x one roll per
// item per trader per restock, uniform within "roll" either way, the same on both sides of its list.
// What a trader has on its own selling shelf it buys only off-market, at value x "ownShelf", from
// its side budget. "buy" stays at the lists' former level (a fifth of value, the buy spread) until
// the rebalance decides it.
{
	"sell": 1.0,
	"buy": 0.2,
	"roll": 0.25,
	"ownShelf": 0.2,
}
